  <!--
    Not built on Linux (ADR 0012, ADR 0017):
    - MonoDevelop.Debugger/ObjectValue/Mac/*, MonoDevelop.Debugger.VSTextView/QuickInfo/MacDebuggerTooltipWindow.cs,
      MonoDevelop.Debugger/DebuggerCompletionCommandHandler.cs: macOS (AppKit / Xamarin.Mac) object value tree,
      debugger tooltip and its completion key handling. The GTK tree view (ObjectValue/Gtk) is used instead.
    - MonoDevelop.Debugger.VSTextView/**: debugger integration of the Cocoa/WPF VS editor view (glyph margin,
      breakpoint / current-statement taggers and format definitions, pinned watch and exception adornments,
      quick info). It needs ICocoaTextView, IGlyphTag and EditorFormatDefinition, which are not in the
      vendored text-only vs-editor-api subset. The GTK editor (SourceEditor2) provides these features itself
      (breakpoint markers, DebugValueTooltipProvider, pinned watches, ExceptionCaughtMessage).
  -->

